  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Cimetidine is a member of the class of guanidines that consists of guanidine carrying a methyl substituent at position <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>, a cyano group at position <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> and a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo>[</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>methyl</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>imidazol</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>yl</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>methyl</mi><mo>]</mo><mi>sulfanyl</mi><mo>}</mo><mi>ethyl</mi></mrow></math>&nbsp;group at position <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e68052c6-0b78-49ec-bdd5-c9b253ce0441-image.png\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 126px;\" />&nbsp;</p>",
